 So yes — the historical test passes against the unchanged source.\n\nSo my implementation approach should be: ensure the source supports all acceptance criteria (it does), add the L03 test (mine, 7 tests — may be replaced by oracle), spec, and evidence.\n\nBut wait — there's a subtlety. The oracle test might test something the base source doesn't do. Let me check the historical test more carefully indirectly. I shouldn't inspect the hidden oracle. But the manifest describes criteria. Let me verify each acceptance criterion against the current source:\n\n1. lease: pending/suspended → in_progress + steeringLeaseId + merged prompt with results. ✓ (verified by my test)\n2. ack monotonic/idempotent: only matching lease; wrong lease no-op; repeat ack no-op (0 updates). ✓\n3. release: back to pending, next lease takes exactly once; released lease can't ack. ✓\n4. cancel/terminal: delivered/discarded/failed never in pending, never leased. ✓\n5. restart: stale in_progress lease (>5min) re-leasable. ✓\n6. isolation: different requesterSessionKey not crossed. ✓\n\nAll good. The base source already handles all these.\n\nNow, one important detail: the historical acceptance record says the typecheckTest gate had exitCode 2 (nonzero historical gates). So the historical run had a typecheck failure recorded. That's a known nonzero gate. My task's instruction says \"run relevant existing checks that do not install dependencies\". The oracle only runs the L03 test.\n\nLet me now run the checks: the L03 test (done), runtime core typecheck, scoped lint, harness validate/dry-run, comms replay/compare, credential scan, SHA256SUMS.\n\nLet me check availabilities. tsgo:core needs typescript native preview; openclaw_runtime has node_modules junction to shared. Let's try.\n\nActually, the historical note says typecheckTest exitCode 2 — meaning tsgo:core:test failed historically. Let me try running tsgo:core (not test) since the acceptance criterion says \"runtime core 类型\".\n\nLet me proceed